\pard\intbl\itap1\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\b \cf6 \cb7 Code Structure
\f0\b0 \cf0 \cb1 \cell 
\pard\intbl\itap1\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf6 \cb7 Long chains of promises and callbacks, each needing to be aware of the\'a0
\f4\fs26 \cb8 searchId
\f0\fs28 \cb7 \'a0and the\'a0
\f4\fs26 \cb8 filteredLocations
\f0\fs28 \cb7 \'a0data.\cf0 \cb1 \cell 
\pard\intbl\itap1\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf6 \cb7 A clean separation.\'a0
\f4\fs26 \cb8 performSearch
\f0\fs28 \cb7 \'a0handles the immediate UI, and the debounced\'a0
\f4\fs26 \cb8 setTimeout
\f0\fs28 \cb7 \'a0handles the single, final, delayed action (the zoom).\cf0 \cb1 \cell \lastrow\row
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf6 \cb7 \strokec6 In short, you are correct. The functionality is the same, but we replaced a long, complicated, and buggy manual system with a short, simple, and correct industry-standard pattern. This allowed us to delete all the code that was supporting the old, flawed logic.\cb1 \
